  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $1$st row and the $3$rd row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $1$st and the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & \\,{R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$",
